---
title: Quick Start
id: quick-start
order: 2
description: "Run a Grok Build coding agent inside a sandbox, fix a bug in a cloned repo, and stream the diff, in minutes."
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You have an app that already calls "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":", and you have an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"XAI_API_KEY"},{"type":"text","value":" (or\nyou've logged in on grok.com). By the end of this guide a Grok Build agent will\nclone a repo into a Docker sandbox, fix a bug, and stream the resulting "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"git diff"},{"type":"text","value":"\nback to you."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you only want concepts first, read the "},{"type":"link","href":"./overview","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Overview"}]},{"type":"text","value":". Otherwise, start\nhere."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"1-install-the-packages","children":[{"type":"text","value":"1. Install the packages"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"package-manager","mode":"install"},"children":[],"properties":{"data-package-manager-meta":"{\"packagesByFramework\":{\"react\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-grok-build\",\"@tanstack/ai-sandbox\",\"@tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker\"]],\"vue\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-grok-build\",\"@tanstack/ai-sandbox\",\"@tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker\"]],\"solid\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-grok-build\",\"@tanstack/ai-sandbox\",\"@tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker\"]],\"svelte\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-grok-build\",\"@tanstack/ai-sandbox\",\"@tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker\"]],\"preact\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-grok-build\",\"@tanstack/ai-sandbox\",\"@tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker\"]],\"angular\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-grok-build\",\"@tanstack/ai-sandbox\",\"@tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker\"]],\"vanilla\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-grok-build\",\"@tanstack/ai-sandbox\",\"@tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker\"]],\"octane\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-grok-build\",\"@tanstack/ai-sandbox\",\"@tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker\"]]},\"mode\":\"install\"}"}},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai"},{"type":"text","value":": the core "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" pipeline."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-grok-build"},{"type":"text","value":": the Grok Build "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"harness adapter"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-sandbox"},{"type":"text","value":": "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defineSandbox"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defineWorkspace"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withSandbox"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker"},{"type":"text","value":": the Docker "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"provider"}]},{"type":"text","value":" that runs the agent in a\ncontainer."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You'll also need Docker running locally, and the "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grok"},{"type":"text","value":" CLI available in your\nsandbox image"}]},{"type":"text","value":" (the Grok Build harness spawns it inside the sandbox). No Docker?\nSee "},{"type":"link","href":"#no-docker-run-on-your-host","children":[{"type":"text","value":"the local-process alternative"}]},{"type":"text","value":" below. For a\nmicroVM instead of a container, see "},{"type":"link","href":"#docker-sandboxes-microvm-sbx","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Docker Sandboxes"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"2-define-the-sandbox","children":[{"type":"text","value":"2. Define the sandbox"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A sandbox bundles three things: a "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"provider"}]},{"type":"text","value":" (the isolation primitive; here\nDocker), a "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"workspace"}]},{"type":"text","value":" (what the agent sees; here a cloned git repo plus a\nsetup step), and a "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"lifecycle"}]},{"type":"text","value":" (when to reuse, snapshot, and tear it down)."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  createSecrets,\n  defineSandbox,\n  defineWorkspace,\n  githubRepo,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport { dockerSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker'\n\nexport const repoSandbox = defineSandbox({\n  id: 'bug-fixer',\n  provider: dockerSandbox({ image: 'node:22' }),\n  workspace: defineWorkspace({\n    // Where the working tree comes from (shallow clone by default).\n    source: githubRepo({ repo: 'owner/buggy-app' }),\n    packageManager: 'pnpm',\n    // Commands that run once during bootstrap.\n    setup: ['corepack enable', 'pnpm install'],\n    // Injected into the sandbox env at create/resume, never persisted to\n    // snapshots, the sandbox store, or the event log.\n    secrets: createSecrets({\n      XAI_API_KEY: process.env.XAI_API_KEY ?? '',\n    }),\n  }),\n  lifecycle: { reuse: 'thread', snapshot: 'after-setup', keepAlive: '30m' },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"snapshot: 'after-setup'"},{"type":"text","value":" (the default when the provider supports snapshots) means\nthe next run resumes from a post-"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pnpm install"},{"type":"text","value":" snapshot instead of re-cloning and\nre-installing, so only the first run pays the cold-start cost."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For everything "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defineWorkspace()"},{"type":"text","value":" can describe, package manager auto-detection,\nparallel setup groups, clone depth, see "},{"type":"link","href":"./workspace","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Workspace"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"3-call-chat-with-the-harness-adapter","children":[{"type":"text","value":"3. Call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" with the harness adapter"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Grok Build adapter declares that it "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"requires"},{"type":"text","value":" a sandbox capability.\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withSandbox(...)"},{"type":"text","value":" is the middleware that "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"provides"}]},{"type":"text","value":" it: it resumes-or-creates\nthe sandbox, bootstraps the workspace, and tears it down per the lifecycle."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { grokBuildText } from '@tanstack/ai-grok-build'\nimport { withSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport { messages, threadId } from './chat-context'\nimport { repoSandbox } from './sandbox'\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  threadId,\n  adapter: grokBuildText('grok-build'),\n  messages,\n  middleware: [withSandbox(repoSandbox)],\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Here "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"messages"},{"type":"text","value":" is your conversation (e.g. a user turn asking the agent to fix the\nbug), and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"threadId"},{"type":"text","value":" keys the sandbox so the same thread reuses the same container.\nSpawning "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grok"},{"type":"text","value":" happens "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"inside"}]},{"type":"text","value":" the sandbox; its events stream back as normal\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" chunks."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"4-stream-the-result-and-read-the-diff","children":[{"type":"text","value":"4. Stream the result and read the diff"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Harness runs emit standard AG-UI chunks (text, tool calls, reasoning) plus a\nnamespaced "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CUSTOM"},{"type":"text","value":" event. When the run finishes, the Grok Build adapter emits a\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"file.changed"},{"type":"text","value":" event carrying the working-tree "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"git diff"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { stream } from './my-run'\n\nfor await (const chunk of stream) {\n  if (chunk.type === 'TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT') {\n    process.stdout.write(chunk.delta)\n  }\n\n  if (chunk.type === 'CUSTOM' && chunk.name === 'file.changed') {\n    const value = chunk.value\n    if (value !== null && typeof value === 'object' && 'diff' in value) {\n      console.log('\\n--- diff ---\\n')\n      console.log(value.diff)\n    }\n  }\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"That "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"diff"},{"type":"text","value":" is point B: the agent cloned the repo, found the bug, edited the files,\nand you printed the change it made, all without the agent touching your host\nfilesystem."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"no-docker-run-on-your-host","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No Docker? Run on your host"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Swap the provider for the local-process one to skip Docker entirely. It runs the\nagent directly on your host (no isolation), which makes for the fastest dev loop:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"package-manager","mode":"install"},"children":[],"properties":{"data-package-manager-meta":"{\"packagesByFramework\":{\"react\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-sandbox-local-process\"]],\"vue\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-sandbox-local-process\"]],\"solid\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-sandbox-local-process\"]],\"svelte\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-sandbox-local-process\"]],\"preact\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-sandbox-local-process\"]],\"angular\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-sandbox-local-process\"]],\"vanilla\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-sandbox-local-process\"]],\"octane\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-sandbox-local-process\"]]},\"mode\":\"install\"}"}},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { grokBuildText } from '@tanstack/ai-grok-build'\nimport {\n  defineSandbox,\n  defineWorkspace,\n  githubRepo,\n  withSandbox,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport { localProcessSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox-local-process'\nimport { messages } from './chat-context'\n\nexport const repoSandbox = defineSandbox({\n  id: 'bug-fixer',\n  provider: localProcessSandbox({\n    scrubEnv: ['XAI_API_KEY', 'GROK_API_KEY'],\n  }),\n  workspace: defineWorkspace({\n    source: githubRepo({ repo: 'owner/buggy-app' }),\n    setup: ['corepack enable', 'pnpm install'],\n  }),\n  lifecycle: { reuse: 'thread' },\n})\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: grokBuildText('composer-2.5', { authMode: 'host' }),\n  messages,\n  middleware: [withSandbox(repoSandbox)],\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"authMode: 'host'"},{"type":"text","value":" so the adapter uses "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grok login"},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scrubEnv"},{"type":"text","value":" removes\nkeys the host process inherited. Those keys would override the login."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A local-process run can also be a CI runner. That machine has no browser\nlogin. Set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"authMode: 'api-key'"},{"type":"text","value":". Then inject "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"XAI_API_KEY"},{"type":"text","value":" as a workspace\nsecret. The sandbox type does not pick this. See "},{"type":"link","href":"./auth","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Harness Auth"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"docker-sandboxes-microvm-sbx","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Docker Sandboxes microVM (sbx)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you want a hypervisor microVM, use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sbxSandbox()"},{"type":"text","value":". This is not a Docker container."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Install Docker Sandboxes so "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sbx"},{"type":"text","value":" is on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"PATH"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"macOS: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"brew trust docker/tap"},{"type":"text","value":", then "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"brew install docker/tap/sbx"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Windows: enable HypervisorPlatform, then "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"winget install -h Docker.sbx"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Debian or Ubuntu: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"curl -fsSL https://get.docker.com | sudo REPO_ONLY=1 sh"},{"type":"text","value":", then "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"apt-get install docker-sbx"},{"type":"text","value":". Add your user to the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"kvm"},{"type":"text","value":" group."}]}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Run "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sbx login"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Swap the provider. Pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"allowNetwork"},{"type":"text","value":" so "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pnpm install"},{"type":"text","value":" can reach the npm registry. A known adapter such as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grok-build"},{"type":"text","value":" also adds its model API host."}]}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  createSecrets,\n  defineSandbox,\n  defineWorkspace,\n  githubRepo,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport { sbxSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker'\n\nexport const repoSandbox = defineSandbox({\n  id: 'bug-fixer',\n  provider: sbxSandbox({\n    allowNetwork: ['*.npmjs.org', 'registry.npmjs.org'],\n  }),\n  workspace: defineWorkspace({\n    source: githubRepo({ repo: 'owner/buggy-app' }),\n    setup: ['pnpm install'],\n    secrets: createSecrets({\n      XAI_API_KEY: process.env.XAI_API_KEY ?? '',\n    }),\n  }),\n  lifecycle: { reuse: 'thread' },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sbxSandbox()"},{"type":"text","value":" always clones a Git repo into the VM. It does not snapshot. Resume is by sandbox name."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"run-the-working-example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Run the working example"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A complete, runnable app ships at\n"},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/tree/main/examples/sandbox-web","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"examples/sandbox-web"}]},{"type":"text","value":".\nThat app is a \"build me an app\" agent (Claude Code on a Docker sandbox) with\ndurable, refresh-surviving runs. It scaffolds an app in the sandbox, runs the\ndev server, and streams back a live preview URL. For a coding agent running at\nthe edge, with the harness (Claude Code, Codex, Grok Build) picked per run\nfrom the UI, see\n"},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/tree/main/examples/sandbox-cloudflare","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"examples/sandbox-cloudflare"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"From here:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Give the agent your own server-side tools (DB lookups, secrets), see "},{"type":"link","href":"./tools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tools"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Lock down what the agent is allowed to run, see "},{"type":"link","href":"./policy","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Policy"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Watch every file the agent touches as it works, see "},{"type":"link","href":"./events","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Events"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"1-install-the-packages","text":"1. Install the packages","level":2},{"id":"2-define-the-sandbox","text":"2. Define the sandbox","level":2},{"id":"3-call-chat-with-the-harness-adapter","text":"3. Call chat() with the harness adapter","level":2},{"id":"4-stream-the-result-and-read-the-diff","text":"4. Stream the result and read the diff","level":2},{"id":"no-docker-run-on-your-host","text":"No Docker? Run on your host","level":2},{"id":"docker-sandboxes-microvm-sbx","text":"Docker Sandboxes microVM (sbx)","level":2},{"id":"run-the-working-example","text":"Run the working example","level":2}]},"frameworks":["react","vue","solid","svelte","preact","angular","vanilla","octane"],"downloadMarkdown":"\nYou have an app that already calls `chat()`, and you have an `XAI_API_KEY` (or\nyou've logged in on grok.com). By the end of this guide a Grok Build agent will\nclone a repo into a Docker sandbox, fix a bug, and stream the resulting `git diff`\nback to you.\n\nIf you only want concepts first, read the [Overview](./overview). Otherwise, start\nhere.\n\n## 1. Install the packages\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-grok-build @tanstack/ai-sandbox @tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker\nvue: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-grok-build @tanstack/ai-sandbox @tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker\nsolid: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-grok-build @tanstack/ai-sandbox @tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-grok-build @tanstack/ai-sandbox @tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker\npreact: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-grok-build @tanstack/ai-sandbox @tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker\nangular: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-grok-build @tanstack/ai-sandbox @tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-grok-build @tanstack/ai-sandbox @tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker\noctane: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-grok-build @tanstack/ai-sandbox @tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n- `@tanstack/ai`: the core `chat()` pipeline.\n- `@tanstack/ai-grok-build`: the Grok Build **harness adapter**.\n- `@tanstack/ai-sandbox`: `defineSandbox`, `defineWorkspace`, `withSandbox`.\n- `@tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker`: the Docker **provider** that runs the agent in a\n  container.\n\nYou'll also need Docker running locally, and the **`grok` CLI available in your\nsandbox image** (the Grok Build harness spawns it inside the sandbox). No Docker?\nSee [the local-process alternative](#no-docker-run-on-your-host) below. For a\nmicroVM instead of a container, see [Docker Sandboxes](#docker-sandboxes-microvm-sbx).\n\n## 2. Define the sandbox\n\nA sandbox bundles three things: a **provider** (the isolation primitive; here\nDocker), a **workspace** (what the agent sees; here a cloned git repo plus a\nsetup step), and a **lifecycle** (when to reuse, snapshot, and tear it down).\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  createSecrets,\n  defineSandbox,\n  defineWorkspace,\n  githubRepo,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport { dockerSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker'\n\nexport const repoSandbox = defineSandbox({\n  id: 'bug-fixer',\n  provider: dockerSandbox({ image: 'node:22' }),\n  workspace: defineWorkspace({\n    // Where the working tree comes from (shallow clone by default).\n    source: githubRepo({ repo: 'owner/buggy-app' }),\n    packageManager: 'pnpm',\n    // Commands that run once during bootstrap.\n    setup: ['corepack enable', 'pnpm install'],\n    // Injected into the sandbox env at create/resume, never persisted to\n    // snapshots, the sandbox store, or the event log.\n    secrets: createSecrets({\n      XAI_API_KEY: process.env.XAI_API_KEY ?? '',\n    }),\n  }),\n  lifecycle: { reuse: 'thread', snapshot: 'after-setup', keepAlive: '30m' },\n})\n```\n\n`snapshot: 'after-setup'` (the default when the provider supports snapshots) means\nthe next run resumes from a post-`pnpm install` snapshot instead of re-cloning and\nre-installing, so only the first run pays the cold-start cost.\n\nFor everything `defineWorkspace()` can describe, package manager auto-detection,\nparallel setup groups, clone depth, see [Workspace](./workspace).\n\n## 3. Call `chat()` with the harness adapter\n\nThe Grok Build adapter declares that it `requires` a sandbox capability.\n`withSandbox(...)` is the middleware that **provides** it: it resumes-or-creates\nthe sandbox, bootstraps the workspace, and tears it down per the lifecycle.\n\n```ts\nimport { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { grokBuildText } from '@tanstack/ai-grok-build'\nimport { withSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport { messages, threadId } from './chat-context'\nimport { repoSandbox } from './sandbox'\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  threadId,\n  adapter: grokBuildText('grok-build'),\n  messages,\n  middleware: [withSandbox(repoSandbox)],\n})\n```\n\nHere `messages` is your conversation (e.g. a user turn asking the agent to fix the\nbug), and `threadId` keys the sandbox so the same thread reuses the same container.\nSpawning `grok` happens **inside** the sandbox; its events stream back as normal\n`chat()` chunks.\n\n## 4. Stream the result and read the diff\n\nHarness runs emit standard AG-UI chunks (text, tool calls, reasoning) plus a\nnamespaced `CUSTOM` event. When the run finishes, the Grok Build adapter emits a\n`file.changed` event carrying the working-tree `git diff`:\n\n```ts\nimport { stream } from './my-run'\n\nfor await (const chunk of stream) {\n  if (chunk.type === 'TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT') {\n    process.stdout.write(chunk.delta)\n  }\n\n  if (chunk.type === 'CUSTOM' && chunk.name === 'file.changed') {\n    const value = chunk.value\n    if (value !== null && typeof value === 'object' && 'diff' in value) {\n      console.log('\\n--- diff ---\\n')\n      console.log(value.diff)\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThat `diff` is point B: the agent cloned the repo, found the bug, edited the files,\nand you printed the change it made, all without the agent touching your host\nfilesystem.\n\n## No Docker? Run on your host\n\nSwap the provider for the local-process one to skip Docker entirely. It runs the\nagent directly on your host (no isolation), which makes for the fastest dev loop:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai-sandbox-local-process\nvue: @tanstack/ai-sandbox-local-process\nsolid: @tanstack/ai-sandbox-local-process\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai-sandbox-local-process\npreact: @tanstack/ai-sandbox-local-process\nangular: @tanstack/ai-sandbox-local-process\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai-sandbox-local-process\noctane: @tanstack/ai-sandbox-local-process\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n```ts\nimport { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { grokBuildText } from '@tanstack/ai-grok-build'\nimport {\n  defineSandbox,\n  defineWorkspace,\n  githubRepo,\n  withSandbox,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport { localProcessSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox-local-process'\nimport { messages } from './chat-context'\n\nexport const repoSandbox = defineSandbox({\n  id: 'bug-fixer',\n  provider: localProcessSandbox({\n    scrubEnv: ['XAI_API_KEY', 'GROK_API_KEY'],\n  }),\n  workspace: defineWorkspace({\n    source: githubRepo({ repo: 'owner/buggy-app' }),\n    setup: ['corepack enable', 'pnpm install'],\n  }),\n  lifecycle: { reuse: 'thread' },\n})\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: grokBuildText('composer-2.5', { authMode: 'host' }),\n  messages,\n  middleware: [withSandbox(repoSandbox)],\n})\n```\n\nSet `authMode: 'host'` so the adapter uses `grok login`. `scrubEnv` removes\nkeys the host process inherited. Those keys would override the login.\n\nA local-process run can also be a CI runner. That machine has no browser\nlogin. Set `authMode: 'api-key'`. Then inject `XAI_API_KEY` as a workspace\nsecret. The sandbox type does not pick this. See [Harness Auth](./auth).\n\n## Docker Sandboxes microVM (sbx)\n\nIf you want a hypervisor microVM, use `sbxSandbox()`. This is not a Docker container.\n\n1. Install Docker Sandboxes so `sbx` is on `PATH`.\n   - macOS: `brew trust docker/tap`, then `brew install docker/tap/sbx`\n   - Windows: enable HypervisorPlatform, then `winget install -h Docker.sbx`\n   - Debian or Ubuntu: `curl -fsSL https://get.docker.com | sudo REPO_ONLY=1 sh`, then `apt-get install docker-sbx`. Add your user to the `kvm` group.\n2. Run `sbx login`.\n3. Swap the provider. Pass `allowNetwork` so `pnpm install` can reach the npm registry. A known adapter such as `grok-build` also adds its model API host.\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  createSecrets,\n  defineSandbox,\n  defineWorkspace,\n  githubRepo,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport { sbxSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker'\n\nexport const repoSandbox = defineSandbox({\n  id: 'bug-fixer',\n  provider: sbxSandbox({\n    allowNetwork: ['*.npmjs.org', 'registry.npmjs.org'],\n  }),\n  workspace: defineWorkspace({\n    source: githubRepo({ repo: 'owner/buggy-app' }),\n    setup: ['pnpm install'],\n    secrets: createSecrets({\n      XAI_API_KEY: process.env.XAI_API_KEY ?? '',\n    }),\n  }),\n  lifecycle: { reuse: 'thread' },\n})\n```\n\n`sbxSandbox()` always clones a Git repo into the VM. It does not snapshot. Resume is by sandbox name.\n\n## Run the working example\n\nA complete, runnable app ships at\n[`examples/sandbox-web`](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/tree/main/examples/sandbox-web).\nThat app is a \"build me an app\" agent (Claude Code on a Docker sandbox) with\ndurable, refresh-surviving runs. It scaffolds an app in the sandbox, runs the\ndev server, and streams back a live preview URL. For a coding agent running at\nthe edge, with the harness (Claude Code, Codex, Grok Build) picked per run\nfrom the UI, see\n[`examples/sandbox-cloudflare`](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/tree/main/examples/sandbox-cloudflare).\n\nFrom here:\n\n- Give the agent your own server-side tools (DB lookups, secrets), see [Tools](./tools).\n- Lock down what the agent is allowed to run, see [Policy](./policy).\n- Watch every file the agent touches as it works, see [Events](./events).\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Quick Start\nid: quick-start\norder: 2\ndescription: \"Run a Grok Build coding agent inside a sandbox, fix a bug in a cloned repo, and stream the diff, in minutes.\"\n---\n\nYou have an app that already calls `chat()`, and you have an `XAI_API_KEY` (or\nyou've logged in on grok.com). By the end of this guide a Grok Build agent will\nclone a repo into a Docker sandbox, fix a bug, and stream the resulting `git diff`\nback to you.\n\nIf you only want concepts first, read the [Overview](./overview). Otherwise, start\nhere.\n\n## 1. Install the packages\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-grok-build @tanstack/ai-sandbox @tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker\nvue: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-grok-build @tanstack/ai-sandbox @tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker\nsolid: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-grok-build @tanstack/ai-sandbox @tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-grok-build @tanstack/ai-sandbox @tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker\npreact: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-grok-build @tanstack/ai-sandbox @tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker\nangular: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-grok-build @tanstack/ai-sandbox @tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-grok-build @tanstack/ai-sandbox @tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker\noctane: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-grok-build @tanstack/ai-sandbox @tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n- `@tanstack/ai`: the core `chat()` pipeline.\n- `@tanstack/ai-grok-build`: the Grok Build **harness adapter**.\n- `@tanstack/ai-sandbox`: `defineSandbox`, `defineWorkspace`, `withSandbox`.\n- `@tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker`: the Docker **provider** that runs the agent in a\n  container.\n\nYou'll also need Docker running locally, and the **`grok` CLI available in your\nsandbox image** (the Grok Build harness spawns it inside the sandbox). No Docker?\nSee [the local-process alternative](#no-docker-run-on-your-host) below. For a\nmicroVM instead of a container, see [Docker Sandboxes](#docker-sandboxes-microvm-sbx).\n\n## 2. Define the sandbox\n\nA sandbox bundles three things: a **provider** (the isolation primitive; here\nDocker), a **workspace** (what the agent sees; here a cloned git repo plus a\nsetup step), and a **lifecycle** (when to reuse, snapshot, and tear it down).\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  createSecrets,\n  defineSandbox,\n  defineWorkspace,\n  githubRepo,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport { dockerSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker'\n\nexport const repoSandbox = defineSandbox({\n  id: 'bug-fixer',\n  provider: dockerSandbox({ image: 'node:22' }),\n  workspace: defineWorkspace({\n    // Where the working tree comes from (shallow clone by default).\n    source: githubRepo({ repo: 'owner/buggy-app' }),\n    packageManager: 'pnpm',\n    // Commands that run once during bootstrap.\n    setup: ['corepack enable', 'pnpm install'],\n    // Injected into the sandbox env at create/resume, never persisted to\n    // snapshots, the sandbox store, or the event log.\n    secrets: createSecrets({\n      XAI_API_KEY: process.env.XAI_API_KEY ?? '',\n    }),\n  }),\n  lifecycle: { reuse: 'thread', snapshot: 'after-setup', keepAlive: '30m' },\n})\n```\n\n`snapshot: 'after-setup'` (the default when the provider supports snapshots) means\nthe next run resumes from a post-`pnpm install` snapshot instead of re-cloning and\nre-installing, so only the first run pays the cold-start cost.\n\nFor everything `defineWorkspace()` can describe, package manager auto-detection,\nparallel setup groups, clone depth, see [Workspace](./workspace).\n\n## 3. Call `chat()` with the harness adapter\n\nThe Grok Build adapter declares that it `requires` a sandbox capability.\n`withSandbox(...)` is the middleware that **provides** it: it resumes-or-creates\nthe sandbox, bootstraps the workspace, and tears it down per the lifecycle.\n\n```ts\nimport { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { grokBuildText } from '@tanstack/ai-grok-build'\nimport { withSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport { messages, threadId } from './chat-context'\nimport { repoSandbox } from './sandbox'\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  threadId,\n  adapter: grokBuildText('grok-build'),\n  messages,\n  middleware: [withSandbox(repoSandbox)],\n})\n```\n\nHere `messages` is your conversation (e.g. a user turn asking the agent to fix the\nbug), and `threadId` keys the sandbox so the same thread reuses the same container.\nSpawning `grok` happens **inside** the sandbox; its events stream back as normal\n`chat()` chunks.\n\n## 4. Stream the result and read the diff\n\nHarness runs emit standard AG-UI chunks (text, tool calls, reasoning) plus a\nnamespaced `CUSTOM` event. When the run finishes, the Grok Build adapter emits a\n`file.changed` event carrying the working-tree `git diff`:\n\n```ts\nimport { stream } from './my-run'\n\nfor await (const chunk of stream) {\n  if (chunk.type === 'TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT') {\n    process.stdout.write(chunk.delta)\n  }\n\n  if (chunk.type === 'CUSTOM' && chunk.name === 'file.changed') {\n    const value = chunk.value\n    if (value !== null && typeof value === 'object' && 'diff' in value) {\n      console.log('\\n--- diff ---\\n')\n      console.log(value.diff)\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThat `diff` is point B: the agent cloned the repo, found the bug, edited the files,\nand you printed the change it made, all without the agent touching your host\nfilesystem.\n\n## No Docker? Run on your host\n\nSwap the provider for the local-process one to skip Docker entirely. It runs the\nagent directly on your host (no isolation), which makes for the fastest dev loop:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai-sandbox-local-process\nvue: @tanstack/ai-sandbox-local-process\nsolid: @tanstack/ai-sandbox-local-process\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai-sandbox-local-process\npreact: @tanstack/ai-sandbox-local-process\nangular: @tanstack/ai-sandbox-local-process\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai-sandbox-local-process\noctane: @tanstack/ai-sandbox-local-process\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n```ts\nimport { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { grokBuildText } from '@tanstack/ai-grok-build'\nimport {\n  defineSandbox,\n  defineWorkspace,\n  githubRepo,\n  withSandbox,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport { localProcessSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox-local-process'\nimport { messages } from './chat-context'\n\nexport const repoSandbox = defineSandbox({\n  id: 'bug-fixer',\n  provider: localProcessSandbox({\n    scrubEnv: ['XAI_API_KEY', 'GROK_API_KEY'],\n  }),\n  workspace: defineWorkspace({\n    source: githubRepo({ repo: 'owner/buggy-app' }),\n    setup: ['corepack enable', 'pnpm install'],\n  }),\n  lifecycle: { reuse: 'thread' },\n})\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: grokBuildText('composer-2.5', { authMode: 'host' }),\n  messages,\n  middleware: [withSandbox(repoSandbox)],\n})\n```\n\nSet `authMode: 'host'` so the adapter uses `grok login`. `scrubEnv` removes\nkeys the host process inherited. Those keys would override the login.\n\nA local-process run can also be a CI runner. That machine has no browser\nlogin. Set `authMode: 'api-key'`. Then inject `XAI_API_KEY` as a workspace\nsecret. The sandbox type does not pick this. See [Harness Auth](./auth).\n\n## Docker Sandboxes microVM (sbx)\n\nIf you want a hypervisor microVM, use `sbxSandbox()`. This is not a Docker container.\n\n1. Install Docker Sandboxes so `sbx` is on `PATH`.\n   - macOS: `brew trust docker/tap`, then `brew install docker/tap/sbx`\n   - Windows: enable HypervisorPlatform, then `winget install -h Docker.sbx`\n   - Debian or Ubuntu: `curl -fsSL https://get.docker.com | sudo REPO_ONLY=1 sh`, then `apt-get install docker-sbx`. Add your user to the `kvm` group.\n2. Run `sbx login`.\n3. Swap the provider. Pass `allowNetwork` so `pnpm install` can reach the npm registry. A known adapter such as `grok-build` also adds its model API host.\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  createSecrets,\n  defineSandbox,\n  defineWorkspace,\n  githubRepo,\n} from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox'\nimport { sbxSandbox } from '@tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker'\n\nexport const repoSandbox = defineSandbox({\n  id: 'bug-fixer',\n  provider: sbxSandbox({\n    allowNetwork: ['*.npmjs.org', 'registry.npmjs.org'],\n  }),\n  workspace: defineWorkspace({\n    source: githubRepo({ repo: 'owner/buggy-app' }),\n    setup: ['pnpm install'],\n    secrets: createSecrets({\n      XAI_API_KEY: process.env.XAI_API_KEY ?? '',\n    }),\n  }),\n  lifecycle: { reuse: 'thread' },\n})\n```\n\n`sbxSandbox()` always clones a Git repo into the VM. It does not snapshot. Resume is by sandbox name.\n\n## Run the working example\n\nA complete, runnable app ships at\n[`examples/sandbox-web`](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/tree/main/examples/sandbox-web).\nThat app is a \"build me an app\" agent (Claude Code on a Docker sandbox) with\ndurable, refresh-surviving runs. It scaffolds an app in the sandbox, runs the\ndev server, and streams back a live preview URL. For a coding agent running at\nthe edge, with the harness (Claude Code, Codex, Grok Build) picked per run\nfrom the UI, see\n[`examples/sandbox-cloudflare`](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/tree/main/examples/sandbox-cloudflare).\n\nFrom here:\n\n- Give the agent your own server-side tools (DB lookups, secrets), see [Tools](./tools).\n- Lock down what the agent is allowed to run, see [Policy](./policy).\n- Watch every file the agent touches as it works, see [Events](./events).\n"}
